  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\nIssued at 254 PM CDT SAT OCT 10 2026\n\nRadar imagery shows the remnants of Isaias continuing to track\nslowly north-northeastward. The system is weakening, with winds\nmarginally meeting wind advisory criteria. As the low moves out\nof the region late Sunday night into Monday, an upper-level ridge\nwill build across the area, bringing warm and dry weather. Daily\nhigh temperatures are expected to reach the mid-to-upper 80s to\nlow 90s after Monday, with overnight lows in the mid-to-upper 50s\nand low 60s. Highs may approach record levels Tuesday through\nThursday depending on model guidance trends.\n\n16",
